// 1. High-Yield Concept: Cold-related injuries (trench foot, chilblains/pernio, panniculitis, cold urticaria, frostbite) and accidental hypothermia (Swiss staging 1-4, cold diuresis, Osborn J wave, coagulopathy, paradoxical undressing, rewarming-method selection, "no one is dead until warm and dead," K+ >12 futility, DNR override).
// 2. The "Trap": Confusing non-freezing injuries (no cyanosis, no ice crystals) with frostbite; over-aggressive intervention in mild hypothermia (hot bath causing afterdrop / vasodilation); reflexively pacing bradycardia or starting CPR in cold but perfusing patients; declaring death before rewarming.
